 * `scripts/n8n_api.py` reads `N8N_URL` (default `http://127.0.0.1:5679`) and `N8N_API_KEY_FILE` (the path of a one-line file with the n8n API key; required). `N8N_URL` must be an `https` address, or `http` to this computer (any IPv4 address that starts with `127`, `::1`, an IPv4 loopback address written in the `::ffff:` form, or `localhost`, which is exactly what the desk's own `is_loopback_host` accepts): the key is sent in a header, so the script refuses any other address, and one it cannot read, at start (before the key file is opened) with a message that says to use https or an SSH tunnel to `127.0.0.1`. The script also does not follow a redirect from n8n (the key header would go to the new address); it reports the redirect as an error. For `http` to this computer the script ignores the proxy settings of the environment (`HTTP_PROXY`, `no_proxy`): the key header goes straight to this computer and never to a proxy; for `https` those settings are used as usual. Every failure that can come from the address, the key file, the workflow file, the network or n8n's answer ends with a short message and exit code 1 or 2 (never a Python traceback, the key or the body of an answer): n8n not reachable, an answer that is not JSON or is nested too deeply to read, a workflow list with an odd entry, a missing argument, a workflow file that cannot be read (missing, not JSON, nested too deeply, no name), a missing, unreadable or directory key file. A workflow name that the terminal cannot show is printed with `?` in place of the characters it cannot encode. Not covered, so a traceback is possible: Ctrl-C, running out of memory and a closed output pipe. A key file that is empty, longer than 4096 characters, has more than one line, or holds a space, a control character or a character outside printable ASCII is refused at start with a fixed message (the key text is never printed). Network and protocol faults (a bad address, a cut-off answer, a reset) print only the name of the error type, never the address or a header. The address is also refused when it holds a user name part (`@`) or a space, tab or line break, and unless the text between `//` and the first `/` is exactly a host name (letters, digits, dots, hyphens) or a bracketed IPv6 address, optionally followed by one `:port` with a port from 1 to 65535 (so a backslash, a second port, text after a bracket, an empty port and `:0` are refused, and a non-ASCII host name must be given in its ASCII form). n8n's own names such as `N8N_PORT` are n8n's, not this repository's; they appear in `docs/n8n-recipe.md`. `scripts/run_live_check.py` takes command-line flags, not settings names: `--key-file`, `--base-url`, `--ledger`, `--cap-run`, `--cap-total`, `--price-date` and one `--model ID=IN_PRICE,OUT_PRICE` per model, and optionally `--max-tokens`, `--effort`, `--timeout` (see the text at the top of the file). Its exit codes: 0 every call was answered with a label; 1 stopped before calling anything (you did not answer `y`, or there was no terminal); 2 refused at the start (a bad setting, a key file that cannot be read, has more than one line or is shorter than 8 characters, or a spend ledger file that is damaged, too big or not a file: all checked before the question, never printing a path or content; a ledger that does not exist yet is a new ledger) or the spend ledger could not be used during the run; 3 at least one call failed.
