top in the domain; the keys of a dictionary inside node parameters (only the values are cleaned); and, in a node name, an expression that refers to another node by an old name when two names became the same (the second gets ` (2)`). Over-cleaning by design: an address that an expression completes, such as `"http://localhost:5678/x?" + $json.q`, is read as a plain address and loses its `?` and what follows on the same run of characters. Likewise a bare local address, a space and then an e-mail address (`http://localhost jane@example.test`) loses the e-mail address too.
